  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 405.03 Approval Required for New Community Wells and New Small CWSs",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 405.03 Approval Required for New Community Wells and New Small CWSs.\n\n(a) No person shall connect a new or existing well to a small CWS without prior approval obtained in accordance with Env-Dw 302 or Env-Dw 305, as applicable, and this part.\n\n(b) Any existing water supply source for a small CWS that has not previously been approved by the department shall meet the requirements specified in Env-Dw 302 or Env-Dw 305, as applicable.\n\n(c) No person shall commence operation of a small CWS or connect a small CWS to any other PWS without obtaining approval for the final design in accordance with Env-Dw 405.10 and without completing the post-construction procedures required by Env-Dw 405.29.\n\nSource. #14158, eff 12-25-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw400.html"
